Blackdrift: remove the "Report broken site" WebCompat reporter.

Why: the reporter's built-in extension opens https://webcompat.com/issues/new
and posts the page URL plus diagnostic data (browser, device, tracking
protection and page details) to it the moment the menu item is tapped, before
the user has decided to file anything. webcompat.com is run by Mozilla's web
compatibility team, so this is data sent to Mozilla, which Blackdrift promises not
to do. The extension is no longer installed, and webCompatReporterAction()
always returns null, so the browser and custom-tab menus never show the item,
also for an install upgraded from a build that had already registered the
extension. WebCompatFeature (Mozilla's local site interventions) stays.
The upstream unit tests that expect the reporter's action (CustomTabMenuTest,
BrowserMenuTest, MenuMiddlewareTest) are @Ignore'd with a Blackdrift reason, and
the androidTest ThreeDotMainMenuTest no longer checks for the menu item.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

